OL,3,GNEWSASorrow of the children shipped to
OL,4,ACanada all alone
OL,5,
OL,6,FWhen 10-year-old Rose Shapcott and her
OL,7,Fbrother Fred, 14, were orphaned and put
OL,8,Finto a Barnardo's children's home in
OL,9,F1891, little did they know they would
OL,10,Fend up being separated and sent
OL,11,Fthousands of miles away across the
OL,12,FAtlantic.
OL,14,FThe siblings were sent to Canada as
OL,15,Fpart of the British Home Children child
OL,16,Fmigration programme, which saw about
OL,17,F100,000 impoverished children from
OL,18,FBritain sent to overseas colonies
OL,19,Fincluding Canada, between 1869 and the
OL,20,F1940s.
OL,23,APub: 05-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
